Z||000002||Her86GT||12-23-2001||11:46 PM||||According to Copyright law, the only thing that you would need permission for would be the signatures.  For something to be copyrightable, it has to be an original creation, put in tangible form.  This is where the signatures come in.  Regular photos aren't really original creations unless there is a destiguishing feature(original)so they would be hard to prove copyrightable.  Either way to be safe, ask.<P>Just a note as well, for something to be copyrighted, it just has have two characteristics: original piece of work/literature etc and put in tangible form (so others can see/hear it).<BR>It does not have to be registered as copyrighted.  <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mycar2sm.jpg"> ||||reg||1
